bout five heroes at once  knowing what they do or who they are and  what their abilities are or in a  worst-case scenario in a game like  here's the storm you only really have to  no 10 heroes max what's going on in  overwatch you have to have every hero  that could possibly be in the game in  your mind in a much faster match length  so suddenly having two different Reapers  on the battlefield and maybe one is  healing to full when he does Wraith form  and the other has double distance with  his shotguns was very confusing for  players and very overwhelming so we  scrapped the system we also felt that  just player power in general through a  progression system especially when there  was some time investment involved was  not good for the competitive nature of  overwatch so that was system number one  that failed and we took out we talked  about it a little bit at blizzcon in  2014 for those of you that remember then  we went down another path and when I  describe this to you're going to say in  hindsight like of course that's obvious  you know you guys should have never put  in in there in the first place but it  wasn't really obvious to us until we had  put the system in and felt it so the  second system we explored had nothing to  do with player power we wanted to focus  entirely on cosmetic rewards which I'll  touch on a little bit later but what we  did was we created a system where each  hero had a level there was a like a  level / hero and the more you played  matches the more you would level up and  winds were worth more exp than losses  and there was you know certain ways to  gain more exp and as you leveled up a  hero like let's take tracer for example  maybe at level 2 you would unlock some  cosmetic stuff and then at level 3 you'd  unlock more and so on and the heroes  capped out at level 20 in the system it  was cool and it was fun but we we had  this live in the in the blizzard alpha  where all of the employees of Blizzard  were playing the game and immediately it  went south on us very quickly so we  would have these cases of you'd be  playing on temple of Anubis and your  team is pinned down in the sandcrawler  you know you can't even get out of Santa  crawler and you look at over at one of  your teammates and they're playing  Bastion you know they're sieged up  inside the spawn room shooting  the door and very politely tell the  person you know hey dude maybe we should  switch to a class that can get through  the choke and and that person would  they'd even be really reasonable about  like yeah you're totally right it's not  right for the team that I'm on Bastion  right now but I'm so close to my next  unlock I don't want to switch off so the  system turned out to be I would describe  it as a minor disaster the cool part  that came out of it was we came up with  a lot of really compelling cosmetic  stuff that like we had really good  rewards for it that the blizzard  employees were very excited about and  I'm going to leave some of those a  little bit of a mystery for you because  I'd rather you see them in person some  of them there's already been hints out  on the internet like people you know  data mined the build and they saw stuff  like our sprays which I think are really  cool there are these awesome emblems  that you can unlock and you know you can  put them actually in the 3d space in the  level sort of show off things that you  had done so those were part of the  system but we had a lot of other really  really cool stuff as part of that but we  realized that the system was encouraging  the wrong behavior in a game that's  about fluid team composition and hero  swapping that a system that overly  rewarded you sticking on one character  was just bad and wrong so what we want  to do when we we've now taken the game  down it's no longer up the beta is going  to come back hopefully mid-january too  late January if the game's not in a  state that we're happy with it might  take even longer than that we might  spill into februari if needed but what  we want to do is introduce a new  progression system that doesn't overly  reward people hanging on one hero like  sometimes it's okay to reward that  behavior we know that there's a lot of  you who have your main and you really  enjoy playing that one character and we  don't want you to feel bad or wrong  about doing that either but we also  don't want to overly reward that's that  type of thing with a progression or  reward system I had a really interesting  conversation with tom chilton who is the  game director on world of war  craft and he made some awesome points  when talking about progression and  overwatch we were talking about World of  Warcraft Diablo and overwatch and Tom  sort of said you know in games like Oh  world of warcraft and diablo in a lot of  ways those games are about progression  you know whether it be through the  character leveling the character power  or the item acquisition it's the main  motivating factor but unless your game  is inherently about progression you want  to be careful to make sure not to overly  focus players on progression as the  end-all be-all and that's how we feel  about overwatch we feel like we would  like the progression system to be light  cosmetic and almost the way of the game  thanking you for your time in it saying  like hey that's cool we know you've  invested some time in overwatch so we  want to give you these light rewards  that don't overly skew the way that you  play the game in one way or another your  motivation for playing overwatch should  be that it's a fun competitive  multiplayer shooter or not that you're  trying to get more powerful or require a  bunch of items so we're probably going  to take a different route with the  overwatch progression system when we get  back to it we're going to use the time  off we already have ideas of what we  want to try and we're going to use the  time between now and end of January to  explore a bunch of stuff internally  again because we'll learn a lot very  quickly just you know trying ideas out  in the game seeing how they come to  fruition and then if we feel really good  about them then we'll bring the beta  back up and we'll introduce the system  to you guys so I look forward to  hopefully next time talking in more  specifics about what we are doing but I  thought it would be helpful for you to  understand you know why why we're  exploring these different routes with  progression and what sort of went wrong  in the past so when you see the new  system you understand how we got there  anyway thanks as always for all the  feedback and comments we'd love to hear  what you guys think about rewards what  you guys think about progression systems  and we really  hope that you guys have a great winter  break and we'll see you soon probably in  January  you  you  you
 

